      "text": "To find the largest prime divisor of 11! + 12!, we can factor out the common factor of 12! from the expression, which gives us:\n\n11! + 12! = 12! * (1 + 11) = 12! * 12\n\nNow, we can see that the largest prime divisor of 11! + 12! is actually 12 because 12! has already been factored out from the expression.\n\nTherefore, the largest prime divisor of 11! + 12! isboxed{12}.",
